:: Carter Hero's Weakness Intro [nobr]

/* Intro */
Science class is a pretty basic one, with it mainly being a review of the various formulas and procedures you have been learning recently. This leads to a rather uneventful and boring class that is only interrupted near the end when you feel an overexcited poke at your shoulder. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hey! <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$CarterNickname</span>!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> whispers to you a little too loudly. Thankfully, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Mr. Chang</span> is just letting people clean up, so he isn’t really interrupting class. Not that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> would ever THINK of talking during a lecture. You turn to your side and greet <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, asking him what’s up. <br>

    <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                },
                },
            {
                Name: "Carter",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Uniform",
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                },
            },
        ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“What are you doing after school?”</span> He asks with a smile. You shrug, giving your answer or lack there-of, and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> smiles. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Well, I wanted to know if you wanted to come over to play and hang out? If you’re not busy. I’m just going to be bored at home by myself all afternoon.”</span> He pouts a little as you ask him why he is stuck at home by himself. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“There’s this big, dumb thing going on in the city and dad has to help organize police security for it and mom is covering it for her program. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> was originally going to stay home with me, we were going to play superheroes, but he got called in last minute to help his friends with stuff afterschool. It stinks.”</span> He sighs again, slopping down into his desk. <br>
<br>
Though the subject may be a bit touchy, <span style="Color: Yellow">you ask about <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span> and he frowns and blows a raspberry.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“The good part about being home alone is I don’t have to deal with all… that.”</span> You can’t help but chuckle at the face he makes in reference to his twin. <span style="Color: Yellow">You still don’t know the situation between those two, you really haven’t even met his twin brother yet, though you’ve learned it is better not to ask.</span> You think for a moment before suggesting that you may turn up, if you find the chance. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Why can’t you give me a straight answer!?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> sighs, slumping down somehow further in his chair, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Fine! I guess I’ll wallow in my loneliness hoping my FRIEND shows up to save me from dying of boredom.”</span> He can’t help but smile, sitting back up in his chair, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“We can use the entire house in our games, since no one else will be there. It’ll be super fun! Oh! I also got something back from my dad I gotta show you, it’s super cool! If you do, come by my house between 3PM and 5PM!”</span> <br>
<br>
You and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> continue to chat and talk during the brief rest period before class ends. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> <span style="Color: LightGreen">seems very excited about having you over, so you try to remember to come by to not disappoint him.</span> <br>
<<socialChange "Carter" 2>>
<span style="Color: Gold">Quest Gained: "Carter: Hero's Weakness"</span><br>
